136	  // union already covers adds nothing, so a union written with it holds the same values as one without. The checker's
137	  // `"blue" | … | (string & {})` keeps its literals for the reader, so `compare` scores it spelled, not identical. A
138	  // `true`/`false` literal is boolean's, not string's.
139	  // `string & {}` and `string & Record<never, never>` (the `LiteralUnion` spellings) are `string` for this purpose.
